-- Demandé par Tom le 27/10/2026 : version anglaise de l'article sur Éric Fallou (insulte citée en français, sans traduction littérale).
UPDATE "articles" SET "en_title" = '“Sale nègre de merde”: a Carroi player reports racist abuse in Andorra', "en_dek" = 'On Sunday 25 October, during the Ordino-Carroi match (3-2) in the Andorran league, ⭐ Éric Fallou, a Carroi player, says he was the target of racist abuse. Passe D gives him its full support.', "en_body_html" = '<p>It was the 93rd minute. The match was nearly over, and yet everything stopped for him. According to ⭐ Éric Fallou, the Ordino goalkeeper allegedly called him a “sale nègre de merde”, a vile racial slur. Words of staggering violence, spoken on a football pitch, in 2026.</p><p>What followed was chaos. Players from both teams came onto the pitch, tension rose, and the match descended into confusion. A serious point: the referee did not stop the game.</p><h2>Our full support for Éric Fallou</h2><p>At Passe D, we say it plainly: ⭐ Éric Fallou has our full support. No player should ever hear that. Not in the 93rd minute, not in any other. Racism has no place in football, or anywhere else.</p><p>The Carroi president has filed a complaint. If the allegations are proven, we hope the goalkeeper will be punished with the utmost severity. No half-measures, no excuses, no “it was the heat of the moment”.</p><h2>What FIFA''s rules say</h2><p>FIFA has set out a clear framework:</p><ul><li>The FIFA Disciplinary Code (article 15) provides for a suspension of at least 10 matches for a player found guilty of discrimination or racist remarks.</li><li>The three-step procedure gives the referee the power to interrupt the match, then suspend it by sending the teams to the dressing rooms, and finally abandon it if the abuse continues.</li><li>National associations, including the Andorran Football Federation, are required to apply these rules in their own competitions.</li></ul><p>On Sunday, not even the first step was taken. That too will need explaining.</p><h2>We want answers</h2><p>We call on the Andorran Football Federation to open a swift and transparent investigation into the complaint filed by the Carroi president. We call on FIFA, the guarantor of the fight against racism in world football, to follow this case closely and ensure its rules are respected. And we want to know why the referee did not stop the match.</p><p>Football says it stands united against racism. It is time to prove it, in the smaller leagues too, far from the cameras.</p><p><strong>No to racism.</strong> ✊🏿</p><p>— Passe D</p>', "en_published" = true
WHERE "slug" = 'racisme-en-andorre-eric-fallou-denonce-des-insultes-racistes' AND "en_title" = '';
